{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head bc147b4ce21c4cb8bfdeb8b1fa1db1529ea6cdd8, tree d43e21abbc28ab07db746bcbb498349731c0d20e, on builder/ce2-lw1-20261115, all 23 artifacts, for request 4dd8e4c3 under my promise 3609689f and standing da772676. This verdict names both implementations: CE-2 (request 2ed36d70, promise b1a1385d, report bd7aecc7, the CE-2 note, primary) and LW-1 (request aefd3249, promise ffb1bb64, report c351d7a3, the LW-1 note). `gs review --prepare` resolved both bindings and reports at this head, with each request closing on the sealed receipt. I read the head from the shared object store, and I applied the clarification in act 93cb48ea.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- `packages/client/src/reads.ts`, `recoverAbsent`. It acts only on a `prepared`, `sent` or `unknown` record whose latest signing is open and dead. It refuses a creation, a standalone record and a target that is not a scope reference. It requires the record's identity, service, signer, actor, key, target, intent digest, meaning and `notAfter` to agree. It reads the journal with the membership's session only. The first page fixes the head, and every later page reads at that fixed head. Each page must have `whole` coverage and the pinned definition. Each entry must parse canonically, follow the previous one by `seq` and `prev`, pass `isEntryOf` under the admitted genesis, carry a time no earlier than the one before, and not be a `floor`. The cursor must equal the next sequence number and must move forward. Any act with the same actor and key answers `present` and ends nothing. The proof needs the fixed head's entry time at or past the signing's `notAfter`. Any failure returns `unproved` with a local reason and ends nothing.\n- `packages/client/src/custody.ts`, `absentIf`. Under the record's lock it rereads the record and checks the whole snapshot again: index, attempt, intent, meaning, `notAfter`, pin, actor, key, target, an unresolved phase and a dead open latest signing. Only then does it run the old ending code, now `#endAbsent`, which closes the signing and records `unsent` with the head. No scope read runs under the lock. A changed record answers `changed`.\n- `packages/client/src/install-request.ts`. The new branch runs only when the caller passes `recoverAbsent` and custody holds a matching unresolved record with a dead latest signing. After the callback it reads custody again and always returns. It never builds or sends. A missing record answers `not-found`. A terminal record goes through the ordinary `project`, which checks the receipt and reads the exact entry for an acceptance. An unchanged record answers `unproved` or `present`. Any other change answers `changed`. `project` now answers `unsent` with the custody refusal and still treats `folded` as unreadable.\n- `packages/cli/src/application-install-runtime.ts`. CLI install passes `recoverAbsent`. That callback first asks the scope for the Native settlement of the exact kept envelope, then runs the proof. A recovery that does not end the record keeps the lost-reply first line and exit code 1, and adds the reason. `early` adds the new refusals, so they do not list an earlier request.\n- `packages/mcp/src/service.ts`. Only `settle` runs the proof, and only with no Card, an expired record, a non-terminal phase, a scope target and no standalone record. After the proof it reads custody again, reports the current record through the ordinary report, and clears the stale receipt. It replaces the sentence only while the record stays unresolved. An `unsent` ending returns the fixed custody failure, with no Native answer and no receipt. A Card check keeps its exact-envelope resend and runs no proof. MCP install does not pass `recoverAbsent`. Act, create and join now return the same custody failure for an `unsent` record, where they threw before. `docs/mcp.md` and `docs/mcp-tools.json` state that read-session authentication may sign its existing request. The seal rows change for the module and `McpService`, and add `unsentRequest` and `absenceRecovery`.\n- LW-1, `examples/lending/browser/annotations.ts`. `reserve` now says \"You can hold at most two reservations at once. The tool must also be free for that day.\" for `guard-failed`. The text names both conditions and does not claim which guard failed. `type-full` names the eight held reservations. `cancel` keeps its old words, `donate` and `publish` get their own subjects, and the shared `guard-failed` and `bad-field` words no longer name cancelling or text. The definition test asserts the third `reserve` words. No guard, definition, pin, scenario or screen changes.\n- The identifiers. Only the two `presentation` fields of the open Lending 0.4.0 and Counter 0.4.0 change. No file under a `releases/` directory changes, and Grow does not change.\n- Both notes. They keep gate attempt 1 (END f67e825b) and the document and Native follow-up (END 3743d64a) as FAIL. They also keep the three controls.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main ce6f02ba is an ancestor. The 23 artifacts name the head, no path repeats, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only ce6f02ba bc147b4c`. From the gated head 480508d8 to this head only the two notes change.\n- Gate 2, END 97cec6f0. `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-15-ce2-lw1-full-gate-attempt2/gate.log` has SHA-256 93c76571…, and `result.json` has edb3450e…. The log names head 480508d8 and tree 9306be31 with 0 changed files. Kernel, Node 204, Counting 56, Plain 4877 with 1 skipped and Native 1136 with 2 skipped passed, and its last line is \"gate passed\". Scale selected nothing, so no Scale case ran.\n- Card. END 6f299703 records the seven local macOS commands passing at 480508d8. No Linux workflow has run at this head.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 11 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One proof in the client serves both explicit routes: MCP `settle` and repeated CLI install. Custody keeps the lock and the ending, and the reader keeps the scope reads, so no scope read runs under a custody lock. Every route reports the current record through the existing report or `project` code. The old unreadable throw for `unsent` becomes a truthful custody failure, and the Native answer shapes stay unchanged.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding.\n\n- The proof ends a record only when the scope's own verified journal, complete from genesis to a fixed head, holds no act with the actor and key, and the head entry's time has reached the signing's `notAfter`. Ordinary admission refuses an act after its `notAfter`, so the kept envelope cannot enter a later entry. A gap, a filter, a floor, a broken chain, a page that does not move forward, or a head before expiry ends nothing.\n- `absentIf` revalidates the whole snapshot under the lock, so a resend, a new attempt or a settlement that lands during the reads stops the ending.\n- No route signs or submits an ACT during recovery. The CLI install branch returns before build and send. A session request may sign for reading, and the tool description now says so.\n- The record, its capacity charge and the original envelope stay in custody. No timer, sweep or eviction runs.\n- LW-1 changes only presentation words.\n\nOne fact for the record: an `unsent` ending tells the caller not to resend and to use a new key only for a new request. A false ending would invite a second request, so the safety of that advice rests on the admission rule above. Ruling 98c1dba9 requires that scope evidence. The builder's source check in act 30370a58 found no ordinary path that admits a fresh signed act below the existing head time. A future admission path that breaks that rule would make this proof unsound, so a change to act admission needs this proof in its review.\n\nSimplification: no required change. `#endAbsent` gives the old ending and the new proof one body, and install now projects every kept outcome through one `project` function.\n\nQualifications that stand: gate attempt 1 and the follow-up stay FAIL. The proof witnesses use a scripted host, transport and TEST keys, and the default-256 SQLite witness shows its local limit only. It does not show a hosted result, a sealed floor or a cost bound for a larger journal. The Card run is local macOS only. No Linux, hosted, provider or physical-device result follows. This approval authorizes no push, landing, signing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bd7aecc7bf2f56592cfb86c098dd37ce31c09f25","binding":"assigned","head":"bc147b4ce21c4cb8bfdeb8b1fa1db1529ea6cdd8","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3609689f7c22d489c82cbc30c44f63450b3bd659\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b1a1385d80e5c4a0059c35cdb697062d4c56c694\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ffb1bb644c29062e8080a036c032a75467ee474c\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e1b33d0d59e1a855db6d0c455a2053c607f5bd98","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}